 2'","norm_id":"nd9e061f64666e134","priority":0.402,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Author bumps both window-tuning constants by 2; the probe-alarm floor now exceeds the real probe-alarm count and the test fails."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In the Scope bullet, state that the window-tuning change raises only _MIN_EXPECTED_ALARMS (total) by 2 and leaves _MIN_EXPECTED_PROBE_ALARMS at 28.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["6 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable).","AC item 'AC2 - `terraform fmt -check` and `terraform validate` pass in `infra/terraform`.' cites operational evidence (iac) that lives outside the codebase; tag it [non-codebase] — prefix the checkbox text with [non-codebase] so the completion verifier accepts a recorded attestation instead of failing to find code proof.","AC item 'AC5 [non-codebase] - After an operator `terraform apply`, `aws logs tail /rebar/' cites operational evidence (iac) that lives outside the codebase; tag it [non-codebase] — prefix the checkbox text with [non-codebase] so the completion verifier accepts a recorded attestation instead of failing to find code proof.","AC item '- [ ] AC5 [non-codebase] - After an operator `terraform apply`, `aws logs tail /rebar/gerrit-host --' carries a [non-codebase] tag that is not at the start of the checkbox text, so it is treated as untagged and judged by the codebase bar. Move the tag to the start of the checkbox text (`- [ ] [non-codebase] <criterion>`), or put a mere mention of the tag in backticks.","AC item '- [ ] AC6 [non-codebase] - The Route 53 health check reports Healthy, and its alarm is OK while Gerr' carries a [non-codebase] tag that is not at the start of the checkbox text, so it is treated as untagged and judged by the codebase bar. Move the tag to the start of the checkbox text (`- [ ] [non-codebase] <criterion>`), or put a mere mention of the tag in backticks."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State that both new alarms declare an alarm_description heredoc (so _MIN_EXPECTED_ALARM_DESCRIPTIONS can be raised by 2), or drop test_alarm_description_byte_limit.py from the floor-raise set if they do not.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.4947,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["test_alarm_description_byte_limit.py:16 _MIN_EXPECTED_ALARM_DESCRIPTIONS = 35","test_alarm_description_byte_limit.py:119-133 counts only alarm blocks with an alarm_description heredoc","Plan Approach describes the two alarms' metrics/thresholds/actions but not alarm_description"],"finding":"The plan lists tests/unit/test_alarm_description_byte_limit.py among modules whose floor is raised by 2, but that module's floor (_MIN_EXPECTED_ALARM_DESCRIPTIONS=35) counts aws_cloudwatch_metric_alarm resources that carry an alarm_description heredoc. The plan's Approach never states the two new alarms include an alarm_description, so raising this floor by 2 is only valid if both new alarms have heredoc descriptions — an unstated requirement.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc1dfa79fa47ed26f","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope: 'tests/unit/test_alarm_description_byte_limit.py ... raise the alarm-count floors by 2'; Approach AC5 alarm definitions","norm_id":"nb14a9211eb522f08","priority":0.2053,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["New alarms are declared without alarm_description heredocs; raising the floor by 2 makes test_parser_finds_the_alarm_descriptions_it_guards fail."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Verify (against SSM Distributor / describe-document) that the AmazonCloudWatchAgent default version resolved at apply is >= 1.300070.0, and record how that stays true for rebuilt hosts (e.g. note the forward-safety argument or pin a floor version).","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.9,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan quote: 'The Distributor package's default version is 1.300074.1, which is journald-capable (>= 1.300070.0)'","Plan quote: 'action=Install, name=AmazonCloudWatchAgent, version unpinned'","The journald-capability threshold is the plan's own stated root-cause gap: 'The CloudWatch agent could not read journald until v1.300070.0'","Evidence class: Partially-verified (integration exists; the specific resolved default version is unconfirmed from repo)"],"finding":"The plan asserts the AWS-ConfigureAWSPackage Distributor default version for AmazonCloudWatchAgent is 1.300074.1 (journald-capable, >= 1.300070.0) as present-tense fact, but installs the package UNPINNED (version unset). The journald log-shipping capability — the entire point of the plan — depends on whatever default AWS resolves at apply time being >= 1.300070.0. This is an external fact not verifiable from the repo.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f2675803d8cd53a66","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach -> Agent install","norm_id":"nb183cf2fdfd7b5f6","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["AWS changes the Distributor default or a rebuilt host resolves a default < 1.300070.0, and journald collection silently never starts while the association still reports success"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.85,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","a